---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site stores on your device and what it never sends anywhere."
>
  <div class="container prose-page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Short version: nothing you do here leaves your device.</p>

    <h2>What is stored, and where</h2>
    <p>
      Three small settings are kept in your browser's local storage so the site remembers you: your reading
      level, your theme (light or dark) and which topics you have opened or marked complete. They live only in
      this browser on this device. Clearing site data removes them, and the progress menu has a "Reset
      progress" button.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your browser blocks storage, the site still works. It simply forgets your choices when you close the
      page.
    </p>

    <h2>What is not done</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No analytics, no advertising and no tracking scripts.</li>
      <li>No accounts and no cookies set by this site.</li>
      <li>Files you open in the tools are read in your browser and never uploaded.</li>
      <li>Search runs on an index shipped with the site, in your browser.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Optional sync</h2>
    <p>
      An optional way to keep your progress across devices is planned. It would be off by default and would
      ask before sending anything. It does not exist yet, so today nothing is sent.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The pages are served by Firebase Hosting. Like any web host it keeps ordinary server logs of requests,
      which are outside this site's control.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
